{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>On the very day.</b> That same day on which he was commanded — by day and not at night. He was not afraid, neither of the nations nor of the mockers, and so that his enemies and the men of his generation would not say: Had we seen him, we would not have let him circumcise himself and fulfill the commandment of the Omnipresent." "<b>And circumcised.</b> A term of וַיִּפְעַל ('and acted')."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:04.939854400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}